 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Points of finite etale group schemes",
 "statement": "Let $G$ be a finite etale group\nscheme of order $m$ over an algebraically closed field $k$, and\n$k'\\supseteq k$ an extension of algebraically closed fields. Then\n\n$$\n|G(k)|=m,\\qquad G(k)\\xrightarrow{\\ \\sim\\ }G(k').\n$$",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-abelian-varieties/sk-prop-av-finite-etale-points/lem-sc-finite-etale-points.md",
  "place": "node lem-sc-finite-etale-points, order 586"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By [lem-sc-finite-etale-algebra-criterion], the coordinate ring\n$\\Gamma(G,\\mathcal O_G)$ of the finite etale $G$ is a finite product of\nfinite separable field extensions of $k$; since $k$ is algebraically\nclosed each of these extensions equals $k$. Hence\n$G\\cong\\coprod_{i=1}^{m}\\operatorname{Spec}k$ as a $k$-scheme; the\norder of $G$ is the $k$-dimension of its coordinate ring\n([def-sc-group-scheme] fixes the group scheme structure of $G$,\nand $m$ is the order of [def-sc-group-scheme] as in the\nstatement of the lemma), so the disjoint union has $m$ terms. Thus\n$G(k)$ is a set of $m$ points and the canonical map\n$G(k)\\to G(k')$ is a bijection.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-sc-finite-etale-algebra-criterion",
    "def-sc-group-scheme"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
